H1500.definition:
feminine of H1498 (גָּזֵל) and mean the same
{robbery, or (concretely) plunder}
KJV: that (he had robbed) (which he took violently away), spoil, violence.

H1501.definition:
from an unused root meaning to devour;
a kind of locust
KJV: palmer-worm.

H1503.definition:
from an unused root meaning to cut down (trees);
the trunk or stump of atree (as felled or as planted)
KJV: stem, stock.

H1504.definition:
a primitive root;
to cut down or off; (figuratively) to destroy, divide, exclude, or decide
KJV: cut down (off), decree, divide, snatch.

H1505.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1504 (גָּזַר);
to quarry; determine
KJV: cut out, soothsayer.

H1506.definition:
from H1504 (גָּזַר);
something cut off; a portion
KJV: part, piece.

H1507.definition:
the same as H1506 (גֶּזֶר);
Gezer, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gazer, Gezer.

H1508.definition:
feminine of H1506 (גֶּזֶר);
the figure or person (as if cut out); also an inclosure (as separated)
KJV: polishing, separate place.

H1509.definition:
from H1504 (גָּזַר);
a desert (as separated)
KJV: not inhabited.

H1510.definition:
(Aramaic) from H1505 (גְּזַר) (as H1504 (גָּזַר));
a decree
KJV: decree.

H1511.definition:
(in the m patrial from H1507 (גֶּזֶר); a Gezerite (collectively) or inhabitants of Gezer; but better (as in the text) bytransposition גִּזְרִיxlit Girzîy corrected to Gizrîy; patrial of H1630 (גְּרִזִים);
a Grizite (collectively) or member of a native tribe in Palestine
KJV: Gezrites.

H1513.definition:
or (feminine) גַּחֶלֶת; from an unused root meaning to glow or kindle;
an ember
KJV: (burning) coal.

H1514.definition:
from an unused root meaning to burn; flame;
Gacham, a son of Nahor
KJV: Gaham.

H1515.definition:
from an unused root meaning to hide; lurker;
Gachar, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Gahar.

H1516.definition:
or (shortened) גַּי; probably (by transmutation) from the same root as H1466 (גֵּוָה) (abbreviated);
a gorge (from its lofty sides; hence, narrow, but not a gully or winter-torrent)
KJV: valley.

H1517.definition:
probably from H1464 (גּוּד);
a thong (as compressing); by analogy, a tendon
KJV: sinew.

H1518.definition:
or (shortened) גֹּחַ; a primitive root;
to gush forth (as water), generally to issue
KJV: break forth, labor to bring forth, come forth, draw up, take out.

H1519.definition:
(Aramaic) or (shortened) גּוּחַ; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1518 (גִּיחַ)lemma גּיחַ missing vowel, corrected to גִּיחַ;
to rush forth
KJV: strive.

H1520.definition:
from H1518 (גִּיחַ)lemma גּיחַ missing vowel, corrected to גִּיחַ; a fountain;
Giach, a place in Palestine
KJV: Giah.

H1521.definition:
or (shortened) גִּחוֹן; from H1518 (גִּיחַ)lemma גּיחַ missing vowel, corrected to גִּיחַ; stream;
Gichon, a river of Paradise; also a valley (or pool) near Jerusalem
KJV: Gihon.

H1522.definition:
or גֵּחֲזִי; apparently from H1516 (גַּיְא) and H2372 (חָזָה); valley of a visionary;
Gechazi, the servant of Elisha
KJV: Gehazi.

H1523.definition:
or (by permutation) גּוּל; a primitive root;
properly, to spin round (under the influence of any violent emotion), i.e. usually rejoice, or (as cringing) fear
KJV: be glad, joy, be joyful, rejoice.

H1524.definition:
from H1523 (גִּיל);
a revolution (of time, i.e. an age); also joy
KJV: [idiom] exceedingly, gladness, [idiom] greatly, joy, rejoice(-ing), sort.

H1525.definition:
or גִּילַת; feminine of H1524 (גִּיל);
joy
KJV: joy, rejoicing.

H1526.definition:
patrial from H1542 (גִּלֹה);
a Gilonite or inhabitant of Giloh
KJV: Gilonite.

H1527.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Ginath, an Israelite
KJV: Ginath.

H1528.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1615 (גִּר);
lime
KJV: plaster.

H1529.definition:
from the same as H1487 (גּוּשׁ); lumpish;
Geshan, an Israelite
KJV: Geshan.

H1530.definition:
from H1556 (גָּלַל);
something rolled, i.e. a heap of stone or dung (plural ruins), by analogy, a spring of water (plural waves)
KJV: billow, heap, spring, wave.

H1531.definition:
from H1556 (גָּלַל);
a cup for oil (as round)
KJV: bowl.

H1532.definition:
from an unused root meaning to shave;
a barber
KJV: barber.

H1533.definition:
from H1530 (גַּל) and H1158 (בָּעָה); fountain of ebullition;
Gilboa, a mountain of Palestine
KJV: Gilboa.

H1534.definition:
by reduplication from H1556 (גָּלַל);
a wheel; by analogy, a whirlwind; also dust (as whirled)
KJV: heaven, rolling thing, wheel.

H1535.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1534 (גַּלְגַּל);
a wheel
KJV: wheel.

H1536.definition:
a variation of H1534 (גַּלְגַּל)
{a wheel; by analogy, a whirlwind; also dust (as whirled)}
KJV: wheel.

H1537.definition:
the same as H1536 (גִּלְגָּל) (with the article as a properly, noun);
Gilgal, the name of three places in Palestine
KJV: Gilgal. See also H1019 (בֵּית הַגִּלְגָּל).

H1538.definition:
by reduplication from H1556 (גָּלַל);
a skull (as round); by implication, a head (in enumeration of persons)
KJV: head, every man, poll, skull.

H1539.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to polish;
the (human) skin (as smooth)
KJV: skin.

H1540.definition:
a primitive root;
to denude (especially in a disgraceful sense); by implication, to exile (captives being usually stripped); figuratively, to reveal
KJV: [phrase] advertise, appear, bewray, bring, (carry, lead, go) captive (into captivity), depart, disclose, discover, exile, be gone, open, [idiom] plainly, publish, remove, reveal, [idiom] shamelessly, shew, [idiom] surely, tell, uncover.

H1541.definition:
(Aramaic) or גְּלָא; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1540 (גָּלָה)
{to denude (especially in a disgraceful sense); by implication, to exile (captives being usually stripped); figuratively, to reveal}
KJV: bring over, carry away, reveal.

H1542.definition:
or (fully) גִּילֹה; from H1540 (גָּלָה); open;
Giloh, a place in Palestine
KJV: Giloh.

H1543.definition:
feminine from H1556 (גָּלַל);
a fountain, bowl or globe (all as round)
KJV: bowl, pommel, spring.

H1544.definition:
or (shortened) גִּלֻּל; from H1556 (גָּלַל);
properly, a log (as round); by implication, an idol
KJV: idol.

H1545.definition:
from H1563 (גָּלַם);
clothing (as wrapped)
KJV: clothes.

H1546.definition:
feminine from H1540 (גָּלָה);
captivity; concretely, exiles (collectively)
KJV: (they that are carried away) captives(-ity).

H1547.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1546 (גָּלוּת)
{captivity; concretely, exiles (collectively)}
KJV: captivity.

H1548.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be bald, i.e. (causatively) to shave; figuratively to lay waste
KJV: poll, shave (off).

H1549.definition:
or גִּלְיוֹן; from H1540 (גָּלָה);
a tablet for writing (as bare); by analogy, a mirror (as a plate)
KJV: glass, roll.

H1550.definition:
from H1556 (גָּלַל);
a valve of a folding door (as turning); also a ring (as round)
KJV: folding, ring.

H1551.definition:
or (prolonged) גָּלִילָה; the same as H1550 (גָּלִיל); a circle (with the article);
Galil (as a special circuit) in the North of Palestine
KJV: Galilee.

H1552.definition:
feminine of H1550 (גָּלִיל);
a circuit or region
KJV: border, coast, country.

H1553.definition:
plural of H1552 (גְלִילָה); circles;
Geliloth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Geliloth.

H1554.definition:
plural of H1530 (גַּל); springs;
Gallim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gallim.

H1555.definition:
perhaps from H1540 (גָּלָה); exile;
Goljath, a Philistine
KJV: Goliath.

H1556.definition:
a primitive root;
to roll (literally or figuratively)
KJV: commit, remove, roll (away, down, together), run down, seek occasion, trust, wallow.

H1557.definition:
from H1556 (גָּלַל);
dung (as in balls)
KJV: dung.

H1558.definition:
from H1556 (גָּלַל);
a circumstance (as rolled around); only used adverbially, on account of
KJV: because of, for (sake).

H1559.definition:
from H1556 (גָּלַל), in the sense of H1560 (גְּלָל); great;
Galal, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Galal.

H1560.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H1556 (גָּלַל);
weight or size (as if rolled)
KJV: great.

H1561.definition:
a variation of H1557 (גָּלָל);
dung (plural balls of dung)
KJV: dung.

H1562.definition:
from H1561 (גֵּלֶל); dungy;
Gilalai, an Israelite
KJV: Gilalai.

H1563.definition:
a primitive root;
to fold
KJV: wrap together.

H1564.definition:
from H1563 (גָּלַם);
a wrapped (and unformed mass, i.e. as the embryo)
KJV: substance yet being unperfect.

H1565.definition:
probably by prolonged from H1563 (גָּלַם);
sterile (as wrapped up too hard); figuratively, desolate
KJV: desolate, solitary.

H1566.definition:
a primitive root;
to be obstinate
KJV: (inter-) meddle (with).

H1567.definition:
from H1530 (גַּל) and H5707 (עֵד); heap of testimony;
Galed, a memorial cairn East of the Jordan
KJV: Galeed.

H1568.definition:
probably from H1567 (גַּלְעֵד);
Gilad, a region East of the Jordan; also the name of three Israelites
KJV: Gilead, Gileadite.

H1569.definition:
patronymically from H1568 (גִּלְעָד);
a Giladite or descendant of Gilad
KJV: Gileadite.

H1570.definition:
a primitive root;
probably to caper (as a goat)
KJV: appear.

H1571.definition:
by contraction from an unused root meaning to gather;
properly, assemblage; used only adverbially also, even, yea, though; often repeated as correl. both...and
KJV: again, alike, also, (so much) as (soon), both (so)...and, but, either...or, even, for all, (in) likewise (manner), moreover, nay...neither, one, then(-refore), though, what, with, yea.

H1573.definition:
from H1572 (גָּמָא);
properly, an absorbent, i.e. the bulrush (from its porosity); specifically the papyrus
KJV: (bul-) rush.

H1574.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to grasp;
properly, a span
KJV: cubit.

H1575.definition:
from the same as H1574 (גֹּמֶד);
a warrior (as grasping weapons)
KJV: Gammadims.

H1576.definition:
from H1580 (גָּמַל);
treatment, i.e. an act (of good or ill); by implication, service or requital
KJV: [phrase] as hast served, benefit, desert, deserving, that which he hath given, recompense, reward.

H1577.definition:
passive participle of H1580 (גָּמַל); rewarded;
Gamul, an Israelite
KJV: Gamul. See also H1014 (בֵּית גָּמוּל).

H1578.definition:
feminine of H1576 (גְּמוּל);
meaning the same
KJV: deed, recompense, such a reward.

H1579.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Gimzo, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gimzo.

H1580.definition:
a primitive root;
to treat a person (well or ill), i.e. benefit or requite; by implication (of toil), to ripen, i.e. (specifically) to wean
KJV: bestow on, deal bountifully, do (good), recompense, requite, reward, ripen, [phrase] serve, mean, yield.

H1581.definition:
apparently from H1580 (גָּמַל) (in the sense of labor or burden-bearing);
a camel
KJV: camel.

H1582.definition:
probably from H1581 (גָּמָל); cameldriver;
Gemalli, an Israelite
KJV: Gemalli.

H1583.definition:
from H1580 (גָּמַל) and H410 (אֵל); reward of God;
Gamliel, an Israelite
KJV: Gamaliel.

H1584.definition:
a primitive root;
to end (in the sense of completion or failure)
KJV: cease, come to an end, fail, perfect, perform.

H1585.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1584 (גָּמַר)
{to end (in the sense of completion or failure)}
KJV: perfect.

H1586.definition:
from H1584 (גָּמַר); completion;
Gomer, the name of a son of Japheth and of his descendants; also of a Hebrewess
KJV: Gomer.

H1587.definition:
or גְּמַרְיָהוּ; from H1584 (גָּמַר) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has perfected;
Gemarjah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Gemariah.

H1588.definition:
from H1598 (גָּנַן);
a garden (as fenced)
KJV: garden.

H1589.definition:
a primitive root;
to thieve (literally or figuratively); by implication, to deceive
KJV: carry away, [idiom] indeed, secretly bring, steal (away), get by stealth.

H1590.definition:
from H1589 (גָּנַב);
a stealer
KJV: thief.

H1591.definition:
from H1589 (גָּנַב);
stealing, i.e. (concretely) something stolen
KJV: theft.

H1592.definition:
from H1589 (גָּנַב); theft;
Genubath, an Edomitish prince
KJV: Genubath.

H1593.definition:
feminine of H1588 (גַּן);
a garden
KJV: garden.

H1594.definition:
another form for H1593 (גַּנָּה)
{a garden}
KJV: garden.

H1595.definition:
from an unused root meaning to store;
treasure; by implication, a coffer
KJV: chest, treasury.

H1596.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1595 (גֶּנֶז);
treasure
KJV: treasure.

H1597.definition:
prolonged from H1595 (גֶּנֶז);
a treasury
KJV: treasury.

H1598.definition:
a primitive root;
to hedge about, i.e. (generally) protect
KJV: defend.

H1599.definition:
or גִּנְּתוֹ; from H1598 (גָּנַן); gardener;
Ginnethon or Ginnetho, an Israelite
KJV: Ginnetho, Ginnethon.
